Common Failure Scenarios & Fixes


-> Scenario 1: Elasticsearch Won't Start
Error: bootstrap checks failed: max virtual memory areas vm.max_map_count [65530] is too low
Fix: sudo sysctl -w vm.max_map_count=262144


-> Scenario 2: Logstash Queue Fills Up
Symptoms: High memory, slow ingestion, dropped logs
Fix:

yaml
queue.max.bytes: 4096mb  # Increase from 2GB
queue.max_events: 500000  # Cap events


-> Scenario 3: Mapping Explosion (Too many fields)
Error: Limit of total fields [1000] has been exceeded
Fix:

json
PUT /logs-*/_settings
{
  "index.mapping.total_fields.limit": 2000
}


-> Scenario 4: Filebeat Duplicate Logs
Cause: Registry file deleted or corrupted
Fix:

bash
# Stop filebeat, find last log line
tail -100 /var/log/app.log

# Manually set registry position
filebeat registry set /var/lib/filebeat/registry "last_offset: 1048576"



->Scenario 5: Red Cluster Status
bash
# Find unassigned shards
curl -X GET "localhost:9200/_cat/shards?h=index,shard,prirep,state,node&s=state"

# Force allocate (temporary fix)
curl -X POST "localhost:9200/_cluster/reroute" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d'
{
  "commands": [
    {
      "allocate_empty_primary": {
        "index": "problem-index",
        "shard": 0,
